From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: s6e3had: add the 96 and 48 Hz timings with stock's gamma compensation

Stock's panel device tree has five timings for the S6E3HAD: fhd120hs,
fhd96hs, fhd60hs, fhd60ns and fhd48hs (there is no fhd48ns). Add 96HS and
48HS with their stock on-commands and the VRR sets __ss_vrr() computes for
them with the default LFD dividers: base 96 Hz, LFD 12-96 and 12-48 Hz,
VFP 02 b0.

At 96 and 48 Hz stock corrects the gamma (ss_brightness_gm2_gamma_comp()).
It reads the HS120 normal gamma from the panel's flash once, after the
reset of the first panel on (ss_gm2_gamma_comp_init(), from
ss_panel_on_pre()), adds MTP_OFFSET_96HS_VAL_revC for the brightness level
and writes the result to C6h/C7h with the level's AOR from aor_table_96,
sets 53h and C2h to 20, and turns the gamma and AOR enablers at the end of
the VRR set on. Do the same, in the same order within the brightness
packet. Stock's levels come from a table of WRDISBV values; this driver
writes WRDISBV directly, so the level is the stock one with the highest
WRDISBV not above it. The HBM row of the offsets is not used, as this
driver has no HBM.

If the flash read fails, or the data has bits set above a colour's width
or is all zero, 96 and 48 Hz run with the 120/60 Hz brightness registers
and a warning.

As for the other timings, each new mode's horizontal front porch is
stretched so that MSM runs the lanes at stock's 910 Mbps: 910.49 Mbps at
96 Hz, 909.80 Mbps at 48 Hz. Stock switches timings live through the
brightness packet; here a change is a full modeset, as before.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---

